1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,191
The Ninth Hall is finished: a long curve of plaster over the river gallery, with lamps set into the ribs like fruit. The first night, people speak softly without being told.

2
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:13,191
Sera's students teach the school now. Sera sits at the back and corrects only the guest law, and only when it is rushed. She says a hurried law becomes a slogan.

3
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:14,468
Pema's apprentices walk the hospital row. The oldest of them is called Pema, because the name has become the work. The first Pema sits in the doorway and counts the breaths she can hear.

4
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:14,043
A rim commander orders the night watch to ignore the singing. He says it is a trick, a way to pull sentries onto the stair. The order is repeated at every shift change.

5
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:11,915
Many listen anyway. They do not step onto the stair. They stand with their hands empty and their eyes wet and pretend, afterward, that the wind was dusty.

6
00:15:00,000 --> 00:15:15,745
Jun marries a gardener in the Ninth Hall. Neither map has a form that fits. The house records the marriage in chalk above the cistern, where the steam will soften it and the hand will rewrite it.

7
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:12,340
Lhamo is in her fifties. She teaches the chord to children who have never seen the upper stair. She tells them a door can be quiet without being gone.

8
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:15,319
Guests come into the hall with empty hands. Their weapons, if they still carry the habit of weapons, stay in the camp. The hall does not have a closet for them. That absence is the design.

9
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:13,617
The rim feels the music through boot soles. Imani sets a listener on the rock and watches the needle keep the old interval. One hundred and eight seconds, and between them, voices.

10
00:27:00,000 --> 00:27:17,872
One night every lamp in the hall is lit together. The river takes the light and gives it back in pieces. People who were here for the first cup, and people who were born after the flood, stand in the same gold.
